# DRAFT-libklibc-2.0.14-ohos-clang-malloc-builtins
# 对应人类文档: knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-libklibc-2.0.14-ohos-clang-malloc-builtins.md
# 状态: 草稿，待知识库审核

id:                     DRAFT-libklibc-2.0.14-ohos-clang-malloc-builtins
trigger_tool:           clang|make|conan create
phase:                  testing|runtime
error_signature:        upstream tests: .*failed.*malloctest3|malloctest3.*assert.*p == NULL|malloctest3.*assert.*calloc
severity:               2
category:               ohos, libc, clang, compiler, testing
match_keywords:         libklibc, klibc, malloctest3, malloc(0), calloc overflow, -fno-builtin-malloc, -fno-builtin-calloc, Clang builtins
title:                  Clang malloc/calloc builtins distort libklibc allocator tests; disable only those builtins for upstream test compilation

root_cause:             Clang recognizes malloc/calloc as builtins while compiling malloctest3. On HarmonyOS AArch64 this changes the behavior observed by the test's zero-size malloc and overflow-calloc assertions, so the test exercises compiler assumptions rather than the built libklibc allocator. Disabling only the two builtins makes the unchanged upstream test pass.
affected_scope:         libc implementations whose upstream tests assert implementation-specific malloc(0) or calloc-overflow behavior, when those test sources are compiled by Clang with allocator builtins enabled.
verification_cmd:       MAKEFLAGS= make -j1 test EXTRA_KLIBCCFLAGS="<target flags> -fno-builtin-malloc -fno-builtin-calloc"; execute all 39 usr/klibc/tests programs and require passed=39, failed=0, not_built=0, skipped=0

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           disable-malloc-calloc-builtins-for-upstream-tests
rec_description:        Add -fno-builtin-malloc and -fno-builtin-calloc only to the upstream test build flags so tests call the target allocator and preserve every upstream assertion.
rec_command:            MAKEFLAGS= make -j1 test EXTRA_KLIBCCFLAGS="<target flags> -fno-builtin-malloc -fno-builtin-calloc"
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      test-only-compile-command-wrapper
fallback_description:   If the upstream build cannot accept target-specific test flags, apply the same two flags through a build-local compiler wrapper for the test compilation commands only; do not edit upstream test source.
fallback_command:       MAKEFLAGS= CC=<test-only-wrapper> make -j1 test
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          conan-recipe

forbid_1_pattern:       skip.*malloctest3|disable.*assert|NDEBUG|modify.*malloctest3\.c
forbid_1_reason:        Those actions remove the exact allocator semantics check and can turn a compiler-induced false failure into a false pass.
forbid_1_consequence:   The upstream pass rate becomes invalid and the allocator behavior remains unverified.
forbid_2_pattern:       MAP_NORESERVE.*malloc.*fix|patch.*malloc.*MAP_NORESERVE
forbid_2_reason:        First isolate compiler builtins; in this reproduction the original allocator mmap flags pass malloctest3, so a MAP_NORESERVE allocator patch is unsupported.
forbid_2_consequence:   An unnecessary allocator behavior change obscures the actual test-compilation cause.

principles:
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             DRAFT-ohos-autotools-rpl-malloc
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

